- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1409.2290/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The construction samples a switching gauge first, builds an exact cyclic two-lift, and asks for its normalized integer adjacency eigenvector. Verification uses only the graph and exact integer arithmetic—never the planted answer.

All local gates pass:

- G1: 12/12 certificates verified
- G4: 0/200,000 guesses; exact density \(2^{-70}\)
- G6: four attacks scored 0/8; spectral reference solved 8/8 in 56,001 operations
- G8: 80/80 relabeling checks
- G9(c): 356 characters, 142 elements, 281 operations
- Escalation correctly ends at `n=75`, 297 operations, then returns `cap_bound`

The paper’s literal SBM labels were rejected as the witness because Section 5.1 makes them probabilistic hidden data; the exact specialization instead uses the adjacency-eigenvector method discussed in Section 5.2. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1409.2290)

External qualification remains blocked: the required hardening run was retried, but every OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The transcripts preserve those errors, and `submit.sh` correctly refuses to treat them as model failures. A funded/reset OpenRouter key is required to finish the bare and G9 oracle runs.
