The audit found a real flaw in the existing build: its planted eigenvalue was deliberately dominant, and a mild random-restart majority heuristic recovers the witness on every tested shipping instance. I’m changing the signed lift to the balanced-offset regime, where the target eigenvalue is interior rather than dominant, and replacing the Track-B reference with exact elimination at the specified eigenvalue. This preserves the paper’s spectral object while making the cheap attack panel meaningful.
