codex
A broad small-prime enumeration I started was unnecessarily expensive because the helper rebuilds the graph for every candidate, so I stopped only that audit process. The mandatory self-test had already completed; I’m replacing the extra check with a bounded version that exercises the same uniqueness claim without turning validation into a search benchmark.
exec
/bin/bash -lc "python3 - <<'PY'
import json
import gen_1409_2290 as g
checks=0
for n in (5,7,11):
 half=(n-1)//2
 for t in sorted({1,max(1,half//2),half}):
  for seed in range(3):
   i=g.make_instance(n,seed=seed,negative_offsets=t)
   count=g.enumerate_all(i)
   assert count == 1, (n,t,seed,count)
   checks += 1
print(f'small-prime uniqueness: {checks}/{checks} exact enumerations have one normalized witness')
checks=0
for preset,p in g.DIFFICULTY.items():
 for seed in (0,1,7,99):
  a=g.make_instance(seed=seed,**p)
  b=g.make_instance(seed=seed,**p)
  assert a==b
